---
import { PLATFORM_DESCRIPTION, PLATFORM_NAME } from "astro:env/client";
import ArticleLayout from "#src/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import Link from "#src/components/Link.astro";
---

<ArticleLayout title="About">
  <hgroup class="mbs-1.5 bg-linear-45 from-emerald-400 to-zinc-100 bg-clip-text text-center text-transparent">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold">About {PLATFORM_NAME}</h1>
    <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl">{PLATFORM_DESCRIPTION}</p>
  </hgroup>

  <p class="mbs-4 text-zinc-300">
    Created by <Link href="https://ssbit01.github.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stefan Samson</Link>, <strong
      >profile.rocks</strong
    > was born out of a simple need: the ability to create and publish a fully functional micro-page directly from any device, from a mobile phone
    to a computer, without restrictions.
  </p>

  <p class="my-4 text-zinc-300">
    While existing micropage services typically restrict users to basic links and plain text, <strong>profile.rocks</strong> was designed to support
    rich Markdown formatting, offering greater flexibility and control over content.
  </p>

  <p class="text-zinc-300">
    Furthermore, unlike the majority of closed-source alternatives on the market, <strong>profile.rocks</strong> aims to be open source. Future
    developments will focus on expanding developer tools to support self-hosting, ensuring long-term independence and customization for users.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
